  "id": "bomba_del_chota",
  "name": "Bomba del Chota (Afro-Ecuadorian Chota Valley)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Afro-Ecuadorian song-dance of the Chota-Mira valley on the border of Imbabura and Carchi provinces, kept by the descendants of Africans enslaved on the valley's colonial sugar haciendas. The bomba, a double-headed hand drum that gives the genre its name, plays with guitars, requinto, güiro and maracas under sung verses, while the related banda mocha imitates a brass band with orange leaves, gourds, horns and bass drum. Groups such as Marabú took it onto record. The hand-drum card stands in for the bomba.",
  "recipe": "classic modern bomba del chota, groove Percussion, Latin am branch. solo with instrumental accompaniment, single lead single track no stacking. classical nylon-string guitar, credited requinto hand drum source unspecified, guiro, maracas. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
